   "source": [
    "# JHPC-quantum Quantum and Supercomputing Collaboration Platform Qiskit User Guide\n",
    "\n",
    "# Table of Contents\n",
    " - [1. Introduction](#1-introduction)\n",
    " - [2. What is Qiskit?](#2-what-is-qiskit)\n",
    " - [3. How to Use](#3-how-to-use)\n",
    "   - [3.1. Environment Setup](#31-environment-setup)\n",
    "   - [3.2. Execution](#32-execution)\n",
    "   - [3.3. Using the FireOpal Error Suppression Library](#33-using-the-fireopal-error-suppression-library)\n",
    " - [4. Known Issues and Workarounds](#4-known-issues-and-workarounds)\n",
    "   - [4.1. The Process Does Not Exit on the JHPC-quantum Collaboration Platform](#41-the-process-does-not-exit-on-the-jhpc-quantum-collaboration-platform)\n",
    "   - [4.2. The Process Does Not Exit with FireOpal](#42-the-process-does-not-exit-with-fireopal)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Introduction\n",
    "This document explains how to execute quantum applications on the JHPC-quantum collaboration platform from the supercomputer 'Fugaku' using Qiskit, a quantum software development kit.\n",
    "If you want to view this procedure in a browser, please refer to the following:\n",
    "[jhpc-quantum GitHub](https://github.com/jhpc-quantum)\n",
    "Updates are available in the [release notes](https://github.com/jhpc-quantum/documents/blob/main/releasenotes.md).\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. What is Qiskit?\n",
    "Qiskit is a collection of software tools for executing programs on quantum computers.\n",
    "Within it, the Qiskit SDK is a software development kit for quantum circuits and operations to run on quantum computers. It is open-source software developed by IBM.\n",
    "For more details about Qiskit, please visit the official website: https://www.ibm.com/quantum/qiskit\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. How to Use\n",
    "## 3.1. Environment Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "If the environment is already set up, there is no need to rebuild it.\n",
    "The steps below are common for both the front-end server and compute nodes (Arm) of Fugaku.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1.1. Creating a Working Directory\n",
    "Create a Qiskit directory in any working directory of your choice (\${WORK}):\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "$ mkdir -p ${WORK}/Qiskit\n",
    "$ cd ${WORK}/Qiskit\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1.2. Building a Python Virtual Environment and Installing Packages\n",
    "Use the environment setup script (venv_setup.sh) to create a Python virtual environment and install the required packages.\n",
    "The packages to be installed are Qiskit and related packages, as well as the JHPC-quantum platform extension for Qiskit (qiskit-sqc-runtime).\n",
    "Installation usually takes a few minutes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Copy the environment setup script (venv_setup.sh) and environment variable setup script (config.sh) from the shared directory:\n",
    "(/vol0300/share/ra010014/jhpcq_modules/<***ARCH***>/SDK_latest/<***Qiskit_x.x.x***>)\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: Replace <***ARCH***> with a64fx or x86 according to your environment.\n",
    "Note: Replace <***Qiskit_x.x.x***> with the version you want to use.\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "$ cp -p /vol0300/share/ra010014/jhpcq_modules/<ARCH>/SDK_latest/<Qiskit_x.x.x>/venv_setup.sh .\n",
    "$ cp -p /vol0300/share/ra010014/jhpcq_modules/<ARCH>/SDK_latest/<Qiskit_x.x.x>/config.sh .\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the environment setup script (venv_setup.sh).\n",
    "\n",
    "Example job script (when running on the front-end server):\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "#!/bin/bash\n",
    "#SBATCH -p mem1\n",
    "#SBATCH -n 1\n",
    "#SBATCH --mem 27G\n",
    "#SBATCH --time=00:10:00\n",
    "\n",
    "./venv_setup.sh\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Example job script (when running on the compute node (Arm)):\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "#!/bin/bash\n",
    "#PJM -L \"node=1\"\n",
    "#PJM -L \"rscgrp=small\"\n",
    "#PJM -L \"elapse=00:10:00\"\n",
    "#PJM -x PJM_LLIO_GFSCACHE=/vol000N:/vol0003:/vol0004\n",
    "#PJM -g groupname\n",
    "\n",
    "./venv_setup.sh\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Environment variable setup script (config.sh)\n",
    "When building the environment on Fugaku and executing Qiskit programs, Spack is used to load the necessary packages.\n",
    "The hash values of the Spack packages used in the script below are current as of May 2026.\n",
    "Note: <**x.x.x**>, <**y.y**>, and <**z.z.z**> represent the versions of the software used.\n",
    "The correspondence between environment variables and software is shown below.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Environment Variable | Software Used |\n",
    "|--------|--------|\n",
    "| FRAMEWORK_VERSION | qiskit |\n",
    "| BACKEND_VERSION | qiskit-sqc-runtime |\n",
    "| SQC_VERSION | SQC library |\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "#!/bin/bash\n",
    "\n",
    "# Framework Name\n",
    "FRAMEWORK_NAME=Qiskit\n",
    "# Framework Version\n",
    "FRAMEWORK_VERSION=<x.x.x>\n",
    "# Backend Version\n",
    "BACKEND_VERSION=<y.y>\n",
    "# SQC Library Version\n",
    "SQC_VERSION=<z.z.z>\n",
    "# Architecture\n",
    "ARCH=$(uname -m)\n",
    "if [ \"$ARCH\" = \"x86_64\" ]; then\n",
    "  # Package Name: python\n",
    "  SPACK_PKG=\"python@3.13.5/xwl6x7i\"\n",
    "  # Target Name\n",
    "  TARGET_NAME=x86\n",
    "elif [ \"$ARCH\" = \"aarch64\" ]; then\n",
    "  # Package Name: python, gcc, numpy\n",
    "  SPACK_PKG=\"python@3.13.5/qhm66vh gcc@15.1.0/c3wm4pb py-numpy@2.2.6/ce7iuxj\"\n",
    "  # Target Name\n",
    "  TARGET_NAME=a64fx\n",
    "else\n",
    "  echo \"error ${ARCH} is unknown\"\n",
    "  exit 1\n",
    "fi\n",
    "# Python Virtual Environment Name\n",
    "VENV_NAME=venv_${FRAMEWORK_NAME}_${FRAMEWORK_VERSION}_${BACKEND_VERSION}\n",
    "# Shared Directory\n",
    "SHARE_DIR=/vol0300/share/ra010014/jhpcq_modules/${TARGET_NAME}/SDK/${FRAMEWORK_NAME}_${FRAMEWORK_VERSION}\n",
    "# SQC Library Directory\n",
    "SQC_DIR=/vol0300/share/ra010014/jhpcq_modules/${TARGET_NAME}/SDK/SQC_library_${SQC_VERSION}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "After the environment setup script is executed successfully, a Python virtual environment is created under the Qiskit directory with the following structure, and packages are installed.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "`-- ${WORK}\n",
    "        |-- Qiskit\n",
    "        |    |-- <ARCH>\n",
    "        |    |      `-- ${VENV_NAME} (Python virtual environment)\n",
    "        |    |-- config.sh\n",
    "        |    `-- venv_setup.sh\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3.2. Execution\n",
    "### 3.2.1. Environment Setup\n",
    "The scripts and sample programs used in the following steps are in the shared directory:\n",
    "(/vol0300/share/ra010014/jhpcq_modules/<***ARCH***>/SDK_latest/<***Qiskit_x.x.x***>/samples)\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: Replace <***ARCH***> with a64fx or x86 according to your environment.\n",
    "Note: Replace <***Qiskit_x.x.x***> with the version you want to use.\n",
    "\n",
    "Environment setup script (backend_setup.sh)\n",
    "This script performs the necessary setup and loading operations for running Qiskit programs.\n",
    "Note: Please set /path/to according to your environment.\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "#!/bin/bash\n",
    "\n",
    "# Setting up Remote Procedure Call (RPC)\n",
    "# 1. Set up the IP address of the quantum computer to SQC_RPC_SERVER according to an argument\n",
    "if [ \"$#\" -eq 1 ]; then\n",
    "  QPU=\"$1\"\n",
    "  if [ \"$QPU\" = \"reimei\" ]; then\n",
    "     # The server port number will be changed for different targets\n",
    "     export SQC_RPC_SERVER=ip:port\n",
    "  elif [ \"$QPU\" = \"reimei-simulator\" ]; then\n",
    "     export SQC_RPC_SERVER=ip:port\n",
    "  elif [ \"$QPU\" = \"ibm-kobe-dacc\" ]; then\n",
    "     export SQC_RPC_SERVER=ip:port\n",
    "  else\n",
    "     echo \"invalid qpu $QPU\"\n",
    "  fi\n",
    "else\n",
    " echo \"usage: /path/to/backend_setup.sh <target-qpu-name>\"\n",
    "fi\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Set up environment variables\n",
    "source /path/to/config.sh\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Load related packages with Spack\n",
    "source /vol0004/apps/oss/spack/share/spack/setup-env.sh\n",
    "spack load ${SPACK_PKG}\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Add module paths for the SQC library to the environment variables below\n",
    "export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=${SQC_DIR}/lib:${SQC_DIR}/lib64:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH\n",
    "export PKG_CONFIG_PATH=${SQC_DIR}/lib64/pkgconfig\n",
    "export PATH=${SQC_DIR}/bin:$PATH\n",
    "\n",
    "# 5. Add SQC library paths to the SQC_LIBRARY_PATH environment variable\n",
    "export SQC_LIBRARY_PATH=${SQC_DIR}/lib64\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.2.2. Execution\n",
    "This section explains how to run a sample quantum circuit on the JHPC-quantum collaboration platform.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: Please refer to the table below for the appropriate argument for service.backend and specify the value corresponding to the target system.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Target | Argument for service.backend(name) |\n",
    "|--------|--------|\n",
    "| reimei | qtm_grpc |\n",
    "| reimei-simulator | qtm_sim_grpc |\n",
    "| ibm-kobe-dacc | ibm_sqc |\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: Please refer to the table below for the mode argument of sampler.run to select either synchronous or asynchronous execution.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Execution Type | Argument for sampler.run(mode) |\n",
    "|--------|--------|\n",
    "| Synchronous execution | sync (default) |\n",
    "| Asynchronous execution | async |\n",
    "\n",
    "Sample program for executing a quantum circuit on the JHPC-quantum collaboration platform (sample.py)\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "from qiskit.circuit import QuantumCircuit\n",
    "from qiskit_ibm_runtime import QiskitRuntimeService, SamplerV2\n",
    "\n",
    "# Construct circuit\n",
    "qc = QuantumCircuit(2)\n",
    "qc.h(0)\n",
    "qc.cx(0, 1)\n",
    "qc.measure_all()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get backend\n",
    "service = QiskitRuntimeService(channel=\"jhpc_quantum\")\n",
    "backend = service.backend(name=\"qtm_sim_grpc\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Transpile circuit\n",
    "from qiskit.transpiler import generate_preset_pass_manager\n",
    "pm = generate_preset_pass_manager(target=backend.target, optimization_level=1)\n",
    "isa_circuit = pm.run(qc)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run quantum circuit\n",
    "sampler = SamplerV2(mode=backend)\n",
    "job = sampler.run([isa_circuit], shots=10, mode=\"sync\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show result\n",
    "result = job.result()\n",
    "print(result[0].data.meas.get_counts())\n",
    "print(job.status())\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the script that executes the Qiskit sample program (test.sh).\n",
    "\n",
    "Example job script (when running on the front-end server):\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "#!/bin/bash\n",
    "#SBATCH -p mem1\n",
    "#SBATCH -n 1\n",
    "#SBATCH --mem 27G\n",
    "#SBATCH --time=00:05:00\n",
    "\n",
    "./test.sh\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Example job script (when running on the compute node (Arm)):\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "#!/bin/bash\n",
    "#PJM -L \"node=1\"\n",
    "#PJM -L \"rscgrp=small\"\n",
    "#PJM -L \"elapse=00:05:00\"\n",
    "#PJM -x PJM_LLIO_GFSCACHE=/vol000N:/vol0003:/vol0004\n",
    "#PJM -g groupname\n",
    "\n",
    "./test.sh\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Script that executes the Qiskit sample program (test.sh)\n",
    "Please specify the path to the Python virtual environment built in Section 3.1.2 in place of \"/path/to/\".\n",
    "Please specify one of the following target quantum computers as the argument to backend_setup.sh:\n",
    "* reimei\n",
    "* reimei-simulator\n",
    "* ibm-kobe-dacc\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "#!/bin/bash\n",
    "\n",
    "# Testing\n",
    "# 1. Set up Remote Procedure Call (RPC)\n",
    "source ./backend_setup.sh reimei-simulator\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Activate the Python virtual environment\n",
    "source /path/to/${VENV_NAME}/bin/activate\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Verification test for qiskit-sqc-runtime installation\n",
    "python ./sample.py\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.2.3. Execution Results\n",
    "Examples of sample program execution results in the front-end environment and on the Fugaku compute node (Arm) are shown below.\n",
    "\n",
    "Synchronous execution:\n",
    "```text\n",
    "{'11': 6, '00': 4}\n",
    "JobStatus.DONE\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Asynchronous execution:\n",
    "```text\n",
    "{'11': 6, '00': 4}\n",
    "[['9c1406bb-c03a-4c20-8ea4-7fe62480bdb8', <JobStatus.DONE: 'job has successfully run'>]]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: In the asynchronous case, job.status() returns a list of [job ID, job status] for each executed circuit, with the same number of entries as the number of circuits run.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3.3. Using the FireOpal Error Suppression Library\n",
    "### 3.3.1. Installing FireOpal\n",
    "When installing the FireOpal module, specify the following option when running the environment setup script:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "$ ./venv_setup.sh --enable FireOpal\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.3.2. Execution\n",
    "Please refer to the following link for the FireOpal sample program:\n",
    "https://portal.qc.r-ccs.riken.jp/redmine/projects/jhpc-quantum-help-desk/wiki/Announcements\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Known Issues and Workarounds\n",
    "## 4.1. The Process Does Not Exit on the JHPC-quantum Collaboration Platform\n",
    "When Qiskit is used to execute on a quantum computer of the JHPC-quantum collaboration platform, the result is returned, but the process does not exit.\n",
    "This issue can occur due to a known limitation in the parallel library.\n",
    "\n",
    "The following temporary workarounds are available:\n",
    "- Terminate the job forcibly as soon as the result is returned by using the job time limit or Ctrl+C.\n",
    "- Set one of the following environment variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "    ```bash\n",
    "    $ export OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1\n",
    "    ```\n",
    "\n",
    "    or\n",
    "\n",
    "    ```bash\n",
    "    $ export OMP_NUM_THREADS=1\n",
    "    ```\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4.2. The Process Does Not Exit with FireOpal\n",
    "When Fire Opal is used on the JHPC-quantum collaboration platform with Qiskit, the result is returned, but the process does not exit.\n",
    "\n",
    "The following temporary workarounds are available:\n",
    "* Terminate the job forcibly as soon as the result is returned by using the job time limit or Ctrl+C.\n",
    "* Perform both of the following:\n",
    "  * Set one of the following environment variables:\n",
    "    * ```bash\n",
    "      $ export OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1\n",
    "      ```\n",
    "    * ```bash\n",
    "      $ export OMP_NUM_THREADS=1\n",
    "      ```\n",
    "  * Add a signal-blocking configuration only during initialization of the FireOpalSampler, which is the cause of the issue.\n",
    "    ```diff\n",
    "    +from contextlib import contextmanager\n",
    "    +import signal\n",
    "    +@contextmanager\n",
    "    +def block_signals():\n",
    "    +    sigs = {signal.SIGUSR2}\n",
    "    +    signal.pthread_sigmask(signal.SIG_BLOCK, sigs)\n",
    "    +    try:\n",
    "    +        yield\n",
    "    +    finally:\n",
    "    +        signal.pthread_sigmask(signal.SIG_UNBLOCK, sigs)\n",
    "    +\n",
    "    :(省略)\n",
    "    -sampler = FireOpalSampler(mode=service.backend(\"ibm_sqc\"))\n",
    "    +with block_signals():\n",
    "    +    sampler = FireOpalSampler(mode=service.backend(\"ibm_sqc\"))\n",
    "    :(省略)\n",
    "    ```\n"
   ]
  }
